  "notes": "Quetzalcoatlus: a giant pterosaur about 5 m tall at the head, stalking the grass on all fours. It stands on its forelimbs with each wing finger folded up and back from the hand and the dark membrane bunched between finger and arm; startled, it vaults into the air and flies off on wings about 12 m across. Pale grey with darker wing membranes, a long stiff neck, a huge tapering beak and a reddish crest; slow, solitary and wary of people.",
